# Allowlist for bin/design-tokens.
#
# Format: <path> | <one-line reason>
#   - A path ending in "/" is a directory prefix (every file under it).
#   - Any other path is an exact file match.
#
# Every entry needs a reason that still holds; an entry whose reason has
# expired (the file no longer does what it says) should be deleted, not kept
# "just in case".
#
# Prefer an exact file to a directory, because a directory entry also exempts
# every file added to it later, under a reason that may not apply to them.
# `lib/config/` was measured and rejected on exactly that ground in the fork this
# came from: only `wind_theme.g.dart` is generated, and every other file in that
# directory is hand-authored, so the directory form would have exempted them all
# under a reason that is false for each one.
#
# One entry is the whole list here, and that is the point: this repository is the
# boilerplate, so a fork starts from a clean surface and adds an entry only when it
# has a real reason to.

lib/config/wind_theme.g.dart | generated by design:sync from DESIGN.md; not hand-authored
